OL,3,GNEWSAParents in plea to reverse        
OL,4,Aplayground decline                     
OL,6,FParents are fighting to reverse a      
OL,7,Flong-standing policy which can see the 
OL,8,F"phasing out" of play parks when ageing
OL,9,Fequipment needs renewing.              
OL,11,FIn 2015, the then Labour-led Durham    
OL,12,FCounty Council agreed to end the use of
OL,13,Fcore funding to upgrade some           
OL,14,Fplaygrounds, instead leaving them at   
OL,15,Fthe mercy of seeking cash from other   
OL,16,Fsources.                               
OL,18,FGeoff Knight, a manager at the council,
OL,19,Fdescribed budgets as "very, very       
OL,20,Fmeagre" but said there were no closures
OL,21,Fplanned "any time soon" and the policy 
OL,22,Fwill be looked at again in March.      
OL,23,APub: 25-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
